===Etymology 1===
{{ety|en|id=surprise|:inh|enm:o<id:oh>|text=+|tree=1}}

====Interjection====
{{en-intj}}

# {{n-g|Expression of [[surprise]].}}
#: {{ux|en|'''Oh'''! I didn't see you there.}}
# {{n-g|Expression of [[wonder]], [[amazement]], or [[awe]].}}
#: {{ux|en|'''Oh''', wow! That's amazing.}}
# {{n-g|Expression of [[understanding]], [[affirmation]], [[recognition]], or [[realization]].}}
#: {{ux|en|'''Oh''', so that's how it works.}}
# {{n-g|A word to precede an annoyed remark.}}
#: {{ux|en|'''Oh''', leave me alone.}}
# {{n-g|A word to precede an added or [[offhand]] comment or [[afterthought]].}}
#: {{ux|en|'''Oh''', and don't forget your coat.}}
#: {{ux|en|What if he says, "'''Oh''', I need to see your ID"?}}
# {{n-g|An invocation or address (similar to the [[vocative]] in languages with noun [[declension]]), often with a term of endearment.}}
#: {{ux|en|'''Oh''', [[gosh]].}}
#* '''1998''', Max Martin, ''...Baby One More Time'' (song performed by Britney Spears)
#*: '''Oh''' baby, baby, how was I supposed to know / That something wasn't right here?
# {{lb|en|often|poetic}} {{n-g|Exclamation for drama or emphasis.}}
#: {{ux|en|'''Oh''', when will it end?}}
#* {{RQ:Raleigh Historie of the World|chapter=Preface|page=32|passage='''Oh''' by what plots, by what forſwearings, betrayings, oppreſsions, impriſonments, tortures, poyſonings, and vnder what reaſons of State, and politique ſubteltie, haue theſe forenamed Kings, {{...}} pulled the vengeance of GOD vpon them-ſelues, {{...}}}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1703|author=Lawrence Smith|title=The Evidence of Things Not Seen|page=143
|passage=And '''oh''' how stingingly acute, and pungently grievous and tormentive, are the remembrancing Reflections of a separate uncloathed Soul in the other World, upon a review of its mad Choice, foolish Hopes, fruitless Desires {{...}}}}
# {{n-g|Expression of pain. See [[ouch]].}}
#: {{ux|en|'''Oh'''! That hurt.}}
#* {{RQ:Cleland Fanny Hill|letter=1|page=83|passage="'''Oh'''! '''Oh'''!——I can't bear it————It is too much.——I die.—————I am going——" were ''Polly''{{'}}s expreſſions of extaſy: {{...}}}}
# {{n-g|Space filler or extra syllable, especially in (popular) music.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1968|author=MacKinlay Kantor|title=Beauty Beast|passage=I'm off with the raggle-taggle gypsy-'''oh'''.}}
# {{lb|en|interrogative}} {{n-g|Expression of mild [[scepticism]].}}
#: {{ux|en|"You should watch where you're going!" "'''Oh'''?"}}

=====Alternative forms=====
Particularly in the context of Internet conversations, "oh" is sometimes written with additional Os or Hs - for example, ''ohhh''. See also {{m|en|ooh}}.

